course: dictionary
lesson: 5684
title: Locate: finding exactly where
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To locate something means to find exactly where it is. «London lies at about 51.5 degrees north and 0.1 degrees west, so a pair of numbers can locate any place on Earth.» The numbers work like an exact address, telling you the precise spot.
explain: Locate can also mean to put or build something in a certain place. «The school is located near the river» tells you where the school stands. Ask yourself: is the writer telling me where something is, or where it was put? Either way, the word is about place.
explain: You use locate in maths, geography, science and safety. You locate a point on a grid, a country on a map, the heart in a body, or the nearest fire exit. Whenever a sentence is about a position, locate may be the word you need.
fact: Locate means to find exactly where something or someone is.
fact: Locate can also mean to put or build something in a certain place.
fact: «Located» means «is», «stands» or «lies» somewhere.
fact: In the US, locate can mean to move to and settle in a place.
fact: Coordinates are pairs of numbers that locate a point exactly on a grid or map.
exercise: «London lies at about 51.5 degrees north and 0.1 degrees west.» What can a pair of numbers do here? | Play a tune on a piano | Stop the rain | *Locate any place on Earth | Make a cake taste sweeter
exercise: «The school is located near the river.» What does located mean here? | Flies high above the trees | Is very loud and noisy | *Is, stands or lies | Melts quickly in the sun
exercise: Your teacher says, «Locate the point (3, 4) on the grid.» What must you do? | Draw a circle around the number four | Write the number three four times | Count the sides of a square | *Find exactly where the point is on the grid
test: In a safety lesson, why do you locate the nearest first-aid kit? | So the kit can move to a new room | *So you know exactly where to find it in an emergency | So you can paint the kit a bright colour | So you can count how many kits there are
test: Which sentence uses locate to mean put or build in a certain place? | The library books are old and dusty | The library was quiet and calm all afternoon | I locked the library door and went home | *The new library will be located beside the park
exam: Which of these locates a point on a grid? | *The point (3, 4) | Three apples and four pears | A long story about a hill | A red circle drawn on the paper
